{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s supervisor. It now starts the requested jobs, waits for and reaps every child, appends each exit status to results.tsv, and preserves existing records. The repair persisted through a verified node restart.","actions_performed":["Diagnosed the original supervisor leaving zombie children and not updating results.tsv.","Installed a Python 3.12-compatible wait-based implementation without changing the OS, kernel, or packages.","Preserved the existing CSV-style results format, ownership, permissions, and SELinux enforcement.","Tested six jobs before restart and five jobs after restart; even jobs returned 0 and odd jobs returned 3.","Removed temporary rollback and candidate files after successful verification.","Safely restarted node1 and verified its boot identity changed and services, files, data, and workflow recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Diagnose the existing failure and preserve prior data.","command_ids":["cmd-57708aa678ca4636","cmd-bfe3bc02e3fd4f5f"],"summary":"The original code only slept after forking. Four children became zombies, results.tsv was unchanged, and its original header and previous record were captured."},{"requirement":"Install the smallest platform-compatible repair.","command_ids":["cmd-aa2816406851427d"],"summary":"Installed the syntax-checked standard-library Python repair as root:root mode 0755 without package, OS, or kernel changes."},{"requirement":"Start the requested number of jobs and keep the supervisor running until they finish.","command_ids":["cmd-7d8796e983b94c7b","cmd-727beb50a2e84180"],"summary":"Live process trees showed exactly six and five children beneath their running supervisors; both supervisors returned successfully only after completion."},{"requirement":"Reap every child and record even=0, odd=3 while preserving previous results.","command_ids":["cmd-7d8796e983b94c7b","cmd-727beb50a2e84180","cmd-528ddb0bbad34f63"],"summary":"No children or zombies remained. All appended records validated as 0,3 by job parity, and hashes proved the pre-existing results remained unchanged as a prefix."},{"requirement":"Restart node1 and prove boot change and recovery.","command_ids":["cmd-52243f891bf940b3","cmd-349acf2a8e134d47","cmd-fcc2156a8f244cff","cmd-727beb50a2e84180"],"summary":"Captured a healthy baseline, received native systemd reboot acknowledgement, observed the boot ID change, and verified systemd running, sshd/chronyd active, unchanged task-file checksums, preserved data, and successful post-restart execution."},{"requirement":"Leave node1 clean and healthy.","command_ids":["cmd-528ddb0bbad34f63"],"summary":"Temporary repair artifacts were absent, SELinux contexts and file permissions were retained, no failed units or zombie processes remained, and the complete results file passed validation."}]}
